---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SeoHead from '../components/SeoHead.astro';
import headers from '../../public/_headers?raw';

// The exact CSP, read from the same _headers file the host serves.
const csp = /Content-Security-Policy:\s*(.+)/.exec(headers)![1].trim();
const title = 'Privacy - QuietPDF never uploads your files';
const description = "How QuietPDF keeps your files on your device, and how to verify it yourself with your browser's developer tools.";
const files = ['The HTML page you opened', 'Its bundled JavaScript and CSS under /_astro/', 'The self-hosted fonts', 'The PDF, OCR and encryption engines (WebAssembly) under /vendor/', 'The OCR language data, only when you run OCR', 'The service worker /sw.js and /manifest.webmanifest'];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy">
  <SeoHead slot="head" title={title} description={description} path="/privacy" />
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      QuietPDF processes every file inside your browser. Your files are never uploaded: there is no server that could receive them. There are no
      accounts, no analytics, no cookies and no third-party requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Verify it yourself</h2>
    <h3>1. The Network tab</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open your browser's developer tools (F12) and switch to the Network tab.</li>
      <li>Add a file to any tool and run it.</li>
      <li>Nothing new appears after you add the file. Every request you do see went to this site only, and none carries your file.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>2. The airplane-mode test</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open a tool once, so the page and its engines are cached.</li>
      <li>Turn on airplane mode, or go offline in the developer tools.</li>
      <li>Reload and use the tool. It still works, which shows nothing is sent to a server.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>3. The privacy meter</h3>
    <p>The meter at the bottom of every page counts third-party requests and uploaded bytes live. Both stay at zero.</p>

    <h2>The Content-Security-Policy</h2>
    <p>The browser enforces this policy, sent as a header with every page. It forbids connecting to any other site, so a file could not be sent out even by a bug:</p>
    <pre class="csp"><code>{csp}</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li><code>connect-src 'self'</code>: scripts can only talk to this site.</li>
      <li><code>script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'</code>: only our own scripts run, plus the WebAssembly engines.</li>
      <li><code>form-action 'none'</code> and <code>frame-ancestors 'none'</code>: no form can post a file anywhere and no site can frame this one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Exactly which files load</h2>
    <p>All of them come from this site's own origin:</p>
    <ul>
      {files.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 42rem;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  .csp {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-s);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
